\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23.3}{\ignorespaces A treap holding the sequence a, \dots  , g, drawn at (position, priority): parents lie above their children, and the in-order walk reads the sequence from left to right. Splitting after five elements walks down the path d, f, e across the cut (the red edges) and relinks it: e becomes the right child of d (green), and f, with g, forms the second treap. Merging the two treaps gives back the first picture.}}{324}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:treap}{{23.3}{324}{A treap holding the sequence a, \dots , g, drawn at (position, priority): parents lie above their children, and the in-order walk reads the sequence from left to right. Splitting after five elements walks down the path d, f, e across the cut (the red edges) and relinks it: e becomes the right child of d (green), and f, with g, forms the second treap. Merging the two treaps gives back the first picture}{figure.caption.8}{}}
